                            	  2620: *************************************************************************************
                            	  2621: *
                            	  2622: * this routine evaluates any type of expression. first it pushes an end marker so
                            	  2623: * it knows when the expression has been evaluated, this is a precedence value of zero.
                            	  2624: * next the first value is evaluated, this can be an in line value, either numeric or
                            	  2625: * string, a variable or array element of any type, a function or even an expression
                            	  2626: * in parenthesis. this value is kept in FAC_1
                            	  2627: * after the value is evaluated a test is made on the next BASIC program byte, if it
                            	  2628: * is a comparrison operator i.e. "<", "=" or ">", then the corresponding bit is set
                            	  2629: * in the comparison evaluation flag. this test loops until no more comparrison operators
                            	  2630: * are found or more than one of any type is found. in the last case an error is generated
                            	  2631: 
                            	  2632: * evaluate expression
                            	  2633: 
                            	  2634: LAB_EVEX
